{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"782c666532cd17ba5fb8da38b5eb1a86a9afaf94d1b0ec633ad320b1fa622a5e","slug":"the-semantic-gap","location":"/chapters/ch09_content_analysis/1_the_semantic_gap.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"The Semantic Gap","authors":[{"id":"Roger Weber","name":"Roger Weber"}],"content_includes_title":false,"numbering":{"title":{"offset":2}},"thumbnail":"/mmir-unibasel-hs26/book/build/figure_9_4-a8c6ad7962573023c5745eb7881611cc.png","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"1_the_semantic_gap.md","url":"/mmir-unibasel-hs26/book/build/1_the_semantic_gap-3fa38d7bddfb2bdac46330723698799a.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consider a photo of the Taj Mahal in a large image collection. The Taj Mahal, located in Agra, India, is a mausoleum that Emperor Shah Jahan built in memory of his wife Mumtaz Mahal, who died in 1631. It is one of the most recognized buildings in the world and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Users who look for such a picture type very different queries: “building, outdoor, sky”, “mausoleum, dome, minaret”, “Taj Mahal”, “UNESCO World Heritage Site”, or even “where is Mumtaz Mahal buried?”. A text retrieval system answers each of these queries by matching words. The photo contains no words.","position":{"start":{"line":14,"column":1},"end":{"line":14,"column":1}},"key":"ftK8yheTTP"}],"key":"r7mSexO7Xp"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"From Text to Media","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"wZjDuJ2LmU"}],"identifier":"from-text-to-media","label":"From Text to Media","html_id":"from-text-to-media","implicit":true,"key":"xFz4M4vePZ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text carries its meaning on the surface. Words and sentences are symbols that people invented to express concepts, so a query and a document share the same symbol system. Even the vocabulary mismatch between “heart disease” and “cardiology treatment”, which defeated keyword search for decades, was largely closed by the embeddings of ","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"lUPeZ1g8dt"},{"type":"link","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Semantic Similarity with Transformers","key":"joSql8Tq8E"}],"identifier":"semantic-similarity-with-transformers","label":"semantic-similarity-with-transformers","url":"/semantic-similarity-with-transformers","internal":true,"dataUrl":"/semantic-similarity-with-transformers.json","key":"wdDgUn3CsV"},{"type":"text","value":": the model learned that both phrases mean similar things. In every case, the starting point was a sequence of words.","position":{"start":{"line":18,"column":1},"end":{"line":18,"column":1}},"key":"N1cps6ZE9J"}],"key":"Vs0OkNIRx6"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"An image starts from a grid of light intensities. A photo of 1024 by 768 pixels with three color channels is a list of ","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"i2bymECete"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"1024 \\cdot 768 \\cdot 3 = 2{,}359{,}296","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1024</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>768</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo separator=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">,</mo><mn>359</mn><mo separator=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">,</mo><mn>296</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1024 \\cdot 768 \\cdot 3 = 2{,}359{,}296</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1024</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">768</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8389em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span><span class=\"mord\">359</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span><span class=\"mord\">296</span></span></span></span>","key":"HuL8u8dVfU"},{"type":"text","value":" numbers between 0 and 255. None of these numbers is “dome”, “sky”, or “Taj Mahal”. ","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"kXmjBBIOji"},{"type":"crossReference","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"xUj9UzYEA8"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"ebvYDt2xiq"}],"identifier":"fig-content-semantic-gap","label":"fig-content-semantic-gap","kind":"figure","template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"1","resolved":true,"html_id":"fig-content-semantic-gap","key":"VaQ0FwiCt4"},{"type":"text","value":" contrasts the two views: what the machine processes is a patch of color values, and what the user enters is a list of concepts at very different levels of abstraction.","position":{"start":{"line":20,"column":1},"end":{"line":20,"column":1}},"key":"AA7KZVCtbD"}],"key":"QAzrSyc2G5"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/mmir-unibasel-hs26/book/build/figure_9_4-a8c6ad7962573023c5745eb7881611cc.png","alt":"The semantic gap: the pixel values a machine processes versus the queries a user enters for the same photo.","width":"95%","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"yqm1DxFoSJ","urlSource":"images/figure_9_4.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"fig-content-semantic-gap","identifier":"fig-content-semantic-gap","html_id":"fig-content-semantic-gap","enumerator":"1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"Kozbiv2Mds"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"BtaWmG58ip"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"IViw0vkyWi"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"sPFbRKYqLq"},{"type":"text","value":"The semantic gap: the pixel values a machine processes versus the queries a user enters for the same photo.","position":{"start":{"line":26,"column":1},"end":{"line":26,"column":1}},"key":"FpbuPa3ANa"}],"key":"itaHRZkFvJ"}],"key":"bKXsu9emNl"}],"label":"fig-content-semantic-gap","identifier":"fig-content-semantic-gap","enumerator":"1","html_id":"fig-content-semantic-gap","key":"X2OY5FX2AV"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The ","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"l2DsDV0DK2"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"semantic gap","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"cartNBNPD2"}],"key":"mBOk1aP8bC"},{"type":"text","value":" is the distance between the low-level features that a system can compute from the signal and the high-level concepts that people use to describe and search for content. The term became standard with the survey by Smeulders et al. in 2000, listed in the Further Reading of the chapter summary, but the problem applies to every non-text medium.","position":{"start":{"line":29,"column":1},"end":{"line":29,"column":1}},"key":"rUG3vyn3QT"}],"key":"G8c3pBIvrb"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The queries in ","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"T40XON6Wg4"},{"type":"crossReference","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"sljZb9PyGZ"},{"type":"text","value":"1","key":"bRDDY3POMw"}],"identifier":"fig-content-semantic-gap","label":"fig-content-semantic-gap","kind":"figure","template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"1","resolved":true,"html_id":"fig-content-semantic-gap","key":"Wj8PvxgtwE"},{"type":"text","value":" reveal that the gap has two parts. Concepts such as “building”, “sky”, and “dome” are visible in the image: a system that interprets the pixels well enough can find them. Concepts such as “UNESCO World Heritage Site” or “where is Mumtaz Mahal buried?” are not in the pixels at all. They require knowledge about the world that the photo does not contain. A system can close the first part by analyzing the content; the second part needs context from outside the content. Such context comes from metadata, from the web page around the photo, or from the world knowledge that a large model absorbed during training, as ","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"lYXbJWMODR"},{"type":"link","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multimodal Transformers","key":"iQP8bsCk93"}],"identifier":"content-analysis-transformers","label":"content-analysis-transformers","url":"/multimodal-transformers","internal":true,"dataUrl":"/multimodal-transformers.json","key":"sZCVeHcczx"},{"type":"text","value":" shows.","position":{"start":{"line":31,"column":1},"end":{"line":31,"column":1}},"key":"PSuGSpodhn"}],"key":"lnFGgiGFMa"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Gap Across Modalities","position":{"start":{"line":33,"column":1},"end":{"line":33,"column":1}},"key":"JxKRvARL7B"}],"identifier":"the-gap-across-modalities","label":"The Gap Across Modalities","html_id":"the-gap-across-modalities","implicit":true,"key":"ArjwVBeA85"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The semantic gap appears in every medium, but its shape differs:","position":{"start":{"line":35,"column":1},"end":{"line":35,"column":1}},"key":"XmwJHM37D8"}],"key":"aL1RkWYq4J"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"mQk8uFDZOQ"}],"key":"IQDxicN8XM"},{"type":"text","value":": the gap is small because the symbols already carry meaning. Keyword search bridged it for decades, and embeddings closed most of the remaining vocabulary mismatch.","position":{"start":{"line":37,"column":1},"end":{"line":37,"column":1}},"key":"IUbpwUlanW"}],"key":"Ijy7P1aP1j"}],"key":"S7mqXqfoKq"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Images","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"MfW0uisWiE"}],"key":"matPGyiLOe"},{"type":"text","value":": a blue region can be sky, water, or fabric. Interpreting the pixels requires recognizing objects, scenes, and people, and relating them to each other.","position":{"start":{"line":38,"column":1},"end":{"line":38,"column":1}},"key":"Dy11czR7d8"}],"key":"eHr4rXAwqc"}],"key":"HQxtqBEcHj"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Audio","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"E0LnZFt6Jr"}],"key":"As5WFZNgIL"},{"type":"text","value":": a CD stores 44,100 samples per second and channel, so a three-minute stereo song is ","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"goZDtg5kto"},{"type":"inlineMath","value":"44{,}100 \\cdot 180 \\cdot 2 = 15{,}876{,}000","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"html":"<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>44</mn><mo separator=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo separator=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">,</mo><mn>876</mn><mo separator=\"true\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">,</mo><mn>000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">44{,}100 \\cdot 180 \\cdot 2 = 15{,}876{,}000</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8389em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">44</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span><span class=\"mord\">100</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">180</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8389em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">15</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span><span class=\"mord\">876</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span></span></span></span>","key":"VZnByELETp"},{"type":"text","value":" amplitude values. A user asks for “a sad piano piece” or “the song that is playing right now”.","position":{"start":{"line":39,"column":1},"end":{"line":39,"column":1}},"key":"Da3N4iEDkM"}],"key":"TD8QtuNLqQ"}],"key":"VB5YjFrliC"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":41,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Video","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"BV2RSgmJIW"}],"key":"Cmdu7fQdXP"},{"type":"text","value":": frames, sound, and subtitles unfold together over time. At 25 frames per second, a one-hour film has 90,000 frames, and a user wants the one scene in which a character says a certain sentence.","position":{"start":{"line":40,"column":1},"end":{"line":40,"column":1}},"key":"m7bhIVud7V"}],"key":"kqo21Lr9XQ"}],"key":"UFH0JcTFKE"}],"key":"DSkrhXvr8B"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"For text, the meaning is in the data and needs to be matched. For the other media, the meaning must first be extracted from the data before anything can be matched. This extraction is called ","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"umExVydAM7"},{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"content analysis","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"hM0WSLmk1a"}],"key":"D4wQDDpRjD"},{"type":"text","value":", and it is the subject of this chapter and the chapters that follow.","position":{"start":{"line":42,"column":1},"end":{"line":42,"column":1}},"key":"vJHOJcrS8O"}],"key":"S1XAxPQWhy"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"warning","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The semantic gap is not a vocabulary mismatch","position":{"start":{"line":44,"column":1},"end":{"line":44,"column":1}},"key":"rWftpsWLEK"}],"key":"Qg1E93XaDz"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is tempting to equate the semantic gap with the vocabulary mismatch of text retrieval (“car” versus “automobile”). In text, query and document use the same kind of symbols, and the problem is that different words express the same concept. In images, audio, and video, the document contains no symbols at all. The system must first produce a description before it can face the vocabulary mismatch.","position":{"start":{"line":45,"column":1},"end":{"line":45,"column":1}},"key":"WUK3quGUON"}],"key":"zot6mRryGX"}],"key":"oZ142hXO3e"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why It Matters","position":{"start":{"line":48,"column":1},"end":{"line":48,"column":1}},"key":"WusBlpoQbq"}],"identifier":"why-it-matters","label":"Why It Matters","html_id":"why-it-matters","implicit":true,"key":"GGyhPb6ayf"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Three application areas show why content analysis has become essential.","position":{"start":{"line":50,"column":1},"end":{"line":50,"column":1}},"key":"uRTyrJBj1V"}],"key":"mFRdWmbWgm"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Social media and content platforms.","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"sVuipeeWvX"}],"key":"Gm4NemD9pt"},{"type":"text","value":" Users upload billions of images and videos every day. Early platforms recommended content mostly through collaborative filtering: users who liked the same items in the past get similar suggestions. A new clip has no viewing history yet, so behavioral signals cannot place it. Behavior alone cannot tell whether a clip shows playful kittens or a lion in a documentary. Feed algorithms such as the one behind TikTok combine behavioral signals with content signals: captions, hashtags, the sound track, and visual features of the video itself. The feeds subsection of ","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"S88s2Dp3O8"},{"type":"link","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learning to Rank","key":"gn2UzgjNbX"}],"identifier":"web-search-learning-to-rank","label":"web-search-learning-to-rank","url":"/learning-to-rank","internal":true,"dataUrl":"/learning-to-rank.json","key":"gjL6DDIpEa"},{"type":"text","value":" describes how such feeds are ranked; this chapter is about where the content signals come from.","position":{"start":{"line":52,"column":1},"end":{"line":52,"column":1}},"key":"zmiD8Wqz10"}],"key":"fzFC8vXaI6"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Media archives and newsrooms.","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"uWtaHdA6uQ"}],"key":"uQxjWde9MJ"},{"type":"text","value":" Broadcasters and news agencies hold millions of photos, video clips, audio recordings, and articles collected over decades. ","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"Svs5PuEDCP"},{"type":"crossReference","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"P22eyMIuT0"},{"type":"text","value":"2","key":"VQOfBH4hNX"}],"identifier":"fig-media-archive","label":"fig-media-archive","kind":"figure","template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"2","resolved":true,"html_id":"fig-media-archive","key":"GlimaJC4ET"},{"type":"text","value":" shows the tape archive of the Danish Broadcasting Corporation. When breaking news arrives, editors have minutes to assemble the material. Suppose Roger Federer announces the end of his career. The evening news wants the highlights of 24 years on tour, from the first Wimbledon title to the last match. A sports broadcaster holds millions of hours of video, and thousands of them show Federer playing tennis. Finding clips with Federer is not enough: the editors need the few that are worth showing.","position":{"start":{"line":54,"column":1},"end":{"line":54,"column":1}},"key":"FCyOIO95zH"}],"key":"REDzZY8GdY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Traditionally, archivists answered this question at filing time. For each new clip, they judged its value for future use, described it with keywords such as the names of the people, the event, and the date, and filed it into tagged folders. The folders worked like an inverted file: the folder “Federer” pointed to the clips worth keeping, so an editor could pull the material within minutes. This metadata was of high quality, but production volumes outgrew the cataloguers long ago, and a decision made at filing time cannot anticipate every future question. Modern archives use face recognition to identify people across thousands of hours of footage, scene detection to cut videos into segments, speech-to-text to make interviews searchable, and multimodal embeddings so that a query for “earthquake” finds relevant clips even without a matching keyword.","position":{"start":{"line":56,"column":1},"end":{"line":56,"column":1}},"key":"eKxu2XSJNm"}],"key":"xbRwpQ1jNJ"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/mmir-unibasel-hs26/book/build/figure_9_1-6d979fd15faf9c07915a34d95ce5216a.png","alt":"The tape archive of the Danish Broadcasting Corporation: when breaking news arrives, the right material must come out within minutes.","width":"80%","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"VwCSAZLH6S","urlSource":"images/figure_9_1.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"fig-media-archive","identifier":"fig-media-archive","html_id":"fig-media-archive","enumerator":"2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"xdqm5TLtOX"},{"type":"text","value":"2","key":"xFvxBMaQdv"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"UPjzizHv3B"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"G6xsSfepbs"},{"type":"text","value":"The tape archive of the Danish Broadcasting Corporation: when breaking news arrives, the right material must come out within minutes.","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"YmO0Fy3iuq"}],"key":"EdjUKctsJ4"}],"key":"af3di0hxhx"}],"label":"fig-media-archive","identifier":"fig-media-archive","enumerator":"2","html_id":"fig-media-archive","key":"gQ2uUJMx2F"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"strong","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Music and audio services.","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"key":"UzEZJBdhCb"}],"key":"K3tqz60560"},{"type":"text","value":" Shazam names a song from a few seconds recorded in a noisy bar. Spotify recommends tracks that fit a mood, such as “music for a rainy afternoon”, or that sound like a given song. Both must connect acoustic patterns with what listeners mean, and both return in ","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"key":"ahOQZxEQuK"},{"type":"link","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Time-Based Media and Specialized Solutions","key":"zZHkyeyLhe"}],"identifier":"content-analysis-time-specialized","label":"content-analysis-time-specialized","url":"/time-and-specialized-solutions","internal":true,"dataUrl":"/time-and-specialized-solutions.json","key":"vsMKyayEPl"},{"type":"text","value":".","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"key":"kAvxr7KQuK"}],"key":"iglWKumY24"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ways to Bridge the Gap","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"TJwk9yq9Ct"}],"identifier":"ways-to-bridge-the-gap","label":"Ways to Bridge the Gap","html_id":"ways-to-bridge-the-gap","implicit":true,"key":"Cv4twDkOfv"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Several complementary strategies connect media content with the concepts of the user. They form the road map of this chapter. ","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"GAXgZwU0IS"},{"type":"crossReference","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"K4FzR4GJsS"},{"type":"text","value":"3","key":"pbe1Kl9Wra"}],"identifier":"fig-content-paths","label":"fig-content-paths","kind":"figure","template":"Figure %s","enumerator":"3","resolved":true,"html_id":"fig-content-paths","key":"ol4wG82YwS"},{"type":"text","value":" shows them side by side.","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"rkczavgtrS"}],"key":"JOTGaEqlZq"},{"type":"container","kind":"figure","children":[{"type":"image","url":"/mmir-unibasel-hs26/book/build/figure_9_14-8bfe6b85112e399404299b5e14feda79.png","alt":"Three paths from media content to search: keywords, features, and transformers.","width":"90%","data":{"altTextIsAutoGenerated":true},"key":"ad11T0W0I1","urlSource":"images/figure_9_14.png"},{"type":"caption","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":75,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"captionNumber","kind":"figure","label":"fig-content-paths","identifier":"fig-content-paths","html_id":"fig-content-paths","enumerator":"3","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Figure ","key":"bCyKB6vrko"},{"type":"text","value":"3","key":"FU5YV52a2G"},{"type":"text","value":":","key":"m49NU1uBIJ"}],"template":"Figure %s:","key":"f